{% comment %}
  "Spoken For" strip across the top of a sold guitar's page.

  Sold guitars stay listed — they show what passes through here and keep their
  search traffic — but a shopper should know before swiping through the
  photos. On phones the gallery comes first, and until this strip the only
  "Spoken For" on the page sat below it, beside the price and on the button.

  Uses the same color scheme as the "Spoken For" badges, so it reads as the
  same status. Renders nothing while the guitar is available.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product liquid object

  Usage:
  {% render 'aeonic-sold-strip', product: product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- unless product.available -%}
  <div class="aeonic-sold-strip color-{{ settings.sold_out_badge_color_scheme }}">
    <p class="aeonic-sold-strip__text">
      <strong class="aeonic-sold-strip__label">{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</strong>
      This guitar has found its next home.
    </p>
    <a class="aeonic-sold-strip__link" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">
      See what's in stock <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  {%- style -%}
    .aeonic-sold-strip {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.6rem 1.6rem;
      margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
      padding: 1.1rem 1.6rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .aeonic-sold-strip__text {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
      color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.85);
    }

    .aeonic-sold-strip__label {
      margin-right: 0.8rem;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #e7cc87;
    }

    .aeonic-sold-strip__link {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
      text-underline-offset: 0.3rem;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .aeonic-sold-strip__link:hover {
      color: #e7cc87;
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endunless -%}
